If you use the pomegranate filter for the tomato, the seed
goes with it.

96
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Loma em wê diguherînin, da ku ava paqij derkeve.
 
Therefore we change it, so that clean juice comes out.

97
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Ev makîne di demeke pir kurt de, karekî mezin dike.
 
This machine in a very short time, does a great job.

98
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Yanî karê milet gelek rehet kiriye?
 
I mean it has made people's work very comfortable?

99
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Pir rehet kiriye. Berê jinan bi saetan kar dikirin û destê
wan diêşiyan.
 
It has made it very comfortable. Before women worked for
hours and their hands hurt.

100
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Hinek caran ji ber westanê jin diketin nexweşiyê.
 
Sometimes because of tiredness women fell ill.

101
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Lê niha, tenê tînin û em di deh deqeyan de dikişînin.
 
But now, they just bring it and we extract it in ten
minutes.

102
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:37,000
Her kes razî ye, bi xweşî distînin û diçin.
 
Everyone is satisfied, they take it happily and go.

103
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Qezenca we ji vî karî baş e, debara we pê dibe?
 
Your profit from this work is good, can you make a living
with it?

104
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Şikir, xwedê bereketê tê de çêbike, em pê debara xwe dikin.
 
Thanks, may God put blessings in it, we make our living with
it.

105
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:53,000
Em naxwazin zêde pere ji xelkê bistînin, em qinyat dikin.
 
We don't want to take too much money from the people, we are
contented.

106
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:59,000
Eger xelk ji te razî be, karê te her tim dimeşe.
 
If the people are satisfied with you, your work always runs.

107
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Tu vî karî li yek cîhî dikî an tu digerî?
 
Do you do this work in one place or do you wander?

108
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Ez digerim bira, ez diçim ber deriyê wan.
 
I wander brother, I go to their doors.

109
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Kesên ku hewce bin, telefonê min dikin, ez diçim cem wan.
 
Those who need it, call me, I go to them.

110
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Ez vê makîneyê li ser erebeya xwe datînim û diçim.
 
I put this machine on my cart and go.

111
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Tiştê herî xweş ew e ku tu bi rûkenî li gel milet kar bikî.
 
The most beautiful thing is that you work with the people
with a smiling face.

112
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Çiqas rûyê te xweş be, ew qas xelk tê cem te.
 
The sweeter your face is, the more people come to you.

113
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:39,000
Kesê wexta rûyê wî tirş be, kes hez nake pê re bixebite.
 
When a person's face is sour, no one likes to work with him.

114
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Belê apê min, ev rastiyeke mezin e.
 
Yes my uncle, this is a great truth.

115
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Em di rojê de ji sibehê heta êvarê dixebitin.
 
We work in the day from morning to evening.

116
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:55,000
Westan tune, çimkî makîne dişixule. Em tenê lê dinêrin.
 
There is no tiredness, because the machine works. We just
watch it.

117
00:16:55,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Dema makîne xera bibe, birayê min hosta ye, ew çêdike.
 
When the machine breaks, my brother is a master, he fixes
it.

118
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:07,000
Ev makîne di eslê xwe de me bi xwe çêkiriye.
 
This machine in its origin we built it ourselves.

119
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Yanî ne yê kargehan e, we bi destê xwe çêkiriye?
 
I mean it is not from factories, you made it with your own
hands?

120
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Belê, birayê min zane ye, wî ev makîne çêkiriye.
 
Yes, my brother is knowledgeable, he made this machine.

121
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:23,000
Me hê di wê demê de, li Sûriyê ev tişt dîtibûn.
 
We had already at that time, seen these things in Syria.

122
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:29,000
Û gava ku em hatin vir, me ev sîstem pêk anî.
 
And when we came here, we brought this system to life.

123
00:17:29,000 --> 00:17:33,000
Gelekî baş e apê min, Xwedê quwetê bide te.
 
It is very good my uncle, may God give you strength.

124
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:39,000
Xwedê ji we jî razî be, ez gelekî kêfxweş bûm.
 
May God be pleased with you too, I became very happy.

125
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Hêviya min ew e ku hûn jî di karê xwe de serkeftî bin.
 
My hope is that you too will be successful in your work.

126
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:51,000
Sipas apê Se'dûn, te me pir kêfxweş kir.
 
Thank you uncle Sa'dûn, you made us very happy.

127
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:58,000
Sercava... ez her tim li vir im dema hûn bixwazin.
 
On my eyes (You're welcome)... I am always here when you
want.

128
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Emê vî karî heta dawiya meha dehan bidomînin.
 
We will continue this work until the end of the tenth month.

129
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Piştî wê, êdî em ê vegerin ser karê xwe yê rojane.
 
After that, we will return to our daily work.

130
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Çi dibe bila bibe, divê mirov roniya çavê xwe qezenc bike.
 
Whatever happens, a person must earn the light of their eyes
(livelihood).

131
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:21,000
Bêguman... keda destan pîroz e.
 
Absolutely... manual labor is blessed.

132
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Belê xortê min. Keda tu kesî wenda nabe.
 
Yes my young man. No one's labor goes lost.

133
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Zemanê berê zehmet bû, niha her tişt hêsan bûye.
 
In the old times it was difficult, now everything has become
easy.

134
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:39,000
Lê divê em qedrê vê asaniyê jî bizanibin.
 
But we must also know the value of this ease.

135
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:45,000
Xelkê berê bi rûkenî zehmetî dikişand, niha jî divê em şikir
bikin.
 
The people of the past endured difficulty with a smile, and
now we must give thanks.

136
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Xalo em te zêde nawestînin, karê te baş.
 
Uncle we won't tire you too much, good work.

137
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:56,000
Na xortê min ne westan e, ez bi dîtina we kêfxweş bûm.
 
No my young man it's not a tiredness, I was happy to see
you.

138
00:18:56,000 --> 00:19:02,000
Ev makîne dema ku dişixule, hemû westan diçe.
 
When this machine is working, all tiredness goes away.

139
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:08,000
Em li ber dengê wê, jiyana xwe derbas dikin.
 
We spend our lives alongside its sound.

140
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Êdî em hêdî hêdî ber bi dawiyê ve diçin, gotineke te ya dawî
heye?
 
Now we are slowly approaching the end, do you have a final
word?

141
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Gotina min a dawî, silav û rêz ji bo hemû temaşevanan e.
 
My final word, greetings and respect to all the viewers.

142
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:25,000
Bila her kes bi keda xwe, serbilind be.
 
Let everyone be proud of their own labor.

143
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Û Xwedê bereketê bixe nava mala her kesî.
 
And may God put blessings in everyone's house.

144
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:35,000
Amin, Xwedê ji te razî be apê Se'dûn.
 
Amen, may God be pleased with you uncle Sa'dûn.

145
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Ji we jî xortê min. Bixatirê we.
 
With you too my young man. Goodbye to you.

146
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:45,000
Xatirê te xalo. Em ê paşê dîsa serdana te bikin.
 
Goodbye uncle. We will visit you again later.

147
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Hûn li ser seran û li ser çavan hatin.
 
You came on my head and on my eyes (You are very welcome).

148
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:56,000
Deriyê me hertim ji we re vekiriye.
 
Our door is always open for you.

149
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Sipas dikim. Roja te xweş.
 
I thank you. Have a good day.

150
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:05,000
...erzan, her tişt me heye. Ahlan wa sahlan bi we. Sema'at,
sema'at, sema'at.
 
...cheap, we have everything. Welcome to you all.
Headphones, headphones, headphones.

151
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Ev sema'at belîş in, ehlen wa sehlen ji we re xalo.
 
These headphones are free, welcome to you, uncle.

152
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
Ev bes ên mezin in yan ê biçûk jî amade di cem we hene?
 
Are these only for adults or do you also have small ones
available?

153
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Ê biçûk jî di cem me hene, hemû imkan di cem bive hene.
 
We also have small ones, we have all kinds available.

154
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
Em di xizmeta we de ne, inşallah...
 
We are at your service, God willing...

155
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Em qusûrê nakin înşallah.
 
We won't fall short, God willing.

156
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Va em diqulpin saetan, ha yekî di nav saetan de kamêra..
heye,
 
Here we move to the watches, here is one with a camera
inside...

157
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Ema saetên kevnar in, qisûrên me hebin bila efo kin,
 
But they are old watches, if we have any shortcomings please
forgive us,

158
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Wê didî jî, bila erzan bidin me, xelîk in jî. Ewa xizmetek
e... milet nin,
 
We also give them cheaply, let them buy from us. That is a
service... to the people,

159
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,000
Ji boy miletî tu kîjan xizmetê dikî, em jî xizmetê dikin.
 
For the people, whatever service you do, we also do a
service.

160
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Ev qenaetê min e, û her kes bi dilê xwe dikire, û hazir im,
 
This is my conviction, and everyone buys according to their
heart, and I am ready,

161
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:40,000
...bêguman ez kesî muxalefet nakim. Em kîjan meqesê re...
hazir in.
 
...of course I don't oppose anyone. Whatever purpose... we
are ready.

162
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:47,000
Kêfê we hizra we di nav me de be. Dengekî nizm me jî milet
nîn, bila qe şe'bî Ewropa ra.
 
May your joy and your thoughts be among us. We have a low
voice for the people, let it reach the people of Europe.

163
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:50,000
Bila tişkê ev hes bikin. Ev qedir ke.
 
Let them feel this. Value this.

164
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:53,000
Û qisûrê me heye... ahlan wa sahlan ji we re.
 
And if we have any shortcomings... welcome to you.

165
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:57,000
Xwedê te silamet ke xalo. Xwedê te star ke...
 
May God keep you safe, uncle. May God protect you...

166
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Welleh serê me te û şixulê te bilind e.
 
By God, we are proud of you and your work.

167
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:20,000
Ehlen wa sehlen...
 
Welcome...

168
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:45,000
Here helo?
 
Come on, hello?

169
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,000
Helîl?
 
Halil?

170
00:22:47,000 --> 00:23:07,000
Ha...
 
Yes...

171
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Ev çi cebelat, evan ji we firotine, ne?
 
What are these mounts, you sell these too, right?

172
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:35,000
Ev ji cem xweda pêk anîye.. nîmetek mezin e me dîtiye.. ji
kîjan alî em xizmet kin xizmet e.
 
This has also been provided by God... it's a great blessing
we have found... from whichever side we serve, it is
service.

173
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Xwedê karê we hêsan ke.
 
May God make your work easy.

174
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:38,000
Şaşî ser e, we xurt e.
 
Your enthusiasm is strong.

175
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:40,000
Taze hatim şuxul... taze me dest pê kiriye, ew e me dît.
Tamam.
 
I just came to work... we just started, this is what we saw.
Okay.

176
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:53,000
Bave Hamo, ez dixwazim pirsekê ji te bikim, wekî her car. Tu
rojê çend saetan li ser pêyê xwe yî? Her roj bar... zû tu ji
mal derdikevî. Tê vir te çi dît?
 
Bave Hamo, I want to ask you a question, like always. How
many hours a day are you on your feet? Every day load... you
leave home early. You come here, what did you see?

177
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:56,000
Çi qas saet ser pîyê xwe disekinim?
 
How many hours do I stand on my feet?

178
00:23:56,000 --> 00:24:04,000
Ev a, ev çar saet e. Ev girêdayî wî bûye çar saetan dest pê
kiriye. Heta pêncan ev e halê min.
 
This, it's four hours. It's been connected to this, starting
from four hours. Until five, this is my situation.

179
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:08,000
Sivik e.. avê xwe sivik e.. evê xwe giran e.. ev fransî
giran e..
 
It's light.. this one is light.. this one is heavy.. this
French one is heavy..

180
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:13,000
Çar saetan li ser xwa diçim, ê dî pênc saetan li ser xwa
diçim..
 
I walk around for four hours, then I walk around for five
hours..

181
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:18,000
Heta bikişim. Wekî ferqek.. kîlo kêm e.. giran bûn.. û tişt
bûn..
 
Until I pull it. Like a difference.. the kilos are less..
they were heavy.. and things..

182
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:23,000
Bila tişkî kê be, bila kîlo kêm be.. bes tu zanî dibisin.
 
Let the thing be less, let the kilos be less.. but you know
they press.

183
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:28,000
Naxwe, te got.. Ev him.. nuh e.. ji te..
 
Then, you said.. This is also.. new.. from you..

184
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:43,000
Ev ev... ev, tê da ketî ye. Ne di cem de ye ev. Av têk e
giran be. Ferq di nav da.. kîlo ferq di heman nîne. Bila
giran be, an jî xêr xan e. Bila sivik be.
 
This.. this, it has fallen into it. It's not with us. It
must be heavy. The difference between.. there is no kilo
difference between them. Let it be heavy, or else it is
charity. Let it be light.

185
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:46,000
Ê, me carekê tebeîyet li evê.. em eyarê evan elîmîne.
 
Yes, we once adapted to this.. we got used to their
adjustment.

186
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:51,000
Îşte ev demsîya fransî ye, û el-hemdu lillah em di nav
xebatê de ne.
 
Look, this is the French type, and thank God we are in the
middle of working.

187
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:56,000
Û pir caran, em tavê lê didin. Me heye.. em li benda
firotanê ne.
 
And many times, the sun hits it. We have it.. we are waiting
to sell.

188
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:58,000
Bavê Hamo em spasîya te dikin. Me ezîyet da te.
 
Bave Hamo, we thank you. We troubled you.

189
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:02,000
Saetên te xweş, em hêvî dikin tu dîsa bêyî nav me. Zor spas.
 
Have a good time, we hope you come among us again. Thank you
very much.

190
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:05,000
Ya ehlan wa sahlan bi we. Xwedê we ser firaz bike, inşallah.
 
Welcome to you. May God elevate you, God willing.

191
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:08,000
Xwedê ji we razî be û em pir kêfxweş in di dîtina we.
 
May God be pleased with you and we are very happy to see
you.

192
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:11,000
Ehlen û sehlen ji we re. Dîtiya me xweş e...
 
Welcome to you. Our meeting is pleasant...

193
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:15,000
Xwedê di we re be û qisûra me efû kin me hêja nizanî..
 
May God be with you and forgive our shortcomings, we still
don't know much..

194
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:17,000
Na bira, hûn rûmet in, taca serî ne.
 
No brother, you are an honor, you are the crown of our
heads.

195
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:23,000
Ehlen wa sehlen ji we re, û xwedê pêxember ji miletê me jî
razî bin..
 
Welcome to you, and may God and the prophet be pleased with
our nation as well..

196
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:26,000
Ê we jî razî bin.. û xwedê qenciyê bide..
 
May he be pleased with you too.. and may God give goodness..

197
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:30,000
Û dengekî me bide.. vî miletî ra, ku ev milet mesîr dike,
xizmet dike.
 
And give us a voice.. for this nation, that this nation
continues, it serves.

198
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:33,000
Saetên we gî yan xweş, êvarên we gî yan xweş.
 
May all your hours be pleasant, may all your evenings be
pleasant.

199
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:37,000
Qedrê we giran e, jin û mêr hez dikin.. an ji we re
miletî...
 
Your value is high, men and women love it.. or for you the
nation...

200
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:44,000
Ez dibêjim saetên we giyan xweş. Û mala we ava, ehlan û
sahlan ji we ra, û we her karî.. hev kar e.
 
I say may all your hours be pleasant. And thank you, welcome
to you, and every job of yours.. is a cooperation.

201
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:47,000
Belê temaşevanan me yî hêja... kesê kû vîdyoyê sêr dike..
 
Yes, our dear viewers... whoever watches this video..

202
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:52,000
Çi li xerîbîyê, çi li vir.. kesên kû Efrîn nedîtine.. di
nava vî.. û derveyî Efrînê..
 
Whether in exile, or here.. those who haven't seen Afrin..
in this.. and outside of Afrin..

203
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:57,000
Dimsî hema hûn dagirin, bibin.. da kû hûn jî bibin derbazin
ciyê cem Bavê Hamo bin..
 
Just pour the syrup, take it.. so that you also pass by the
place of Bave Hamo..

204
00:25:57,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Destpêkê dîrok derbaz dibe, wext ê tên li ser pîyê xwe
çapê..
 
First, history passes by, the times come on your running
feet..

205
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:05,000
Bavê Hamo naskirîye, bes we qe nexwestiye derbazî ciyê me
bibin.
 
Bave Hamo is known, but you never wanted to pass by our
place.

206
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:10,000
Û bi qencî ger em we razî nekin wê dighêje dîsa da vîdyokî,
ku hûn di nav de bibînin.
 
And kindly, if we don't satisfy you, it will reach another
video, so you can see it inside.

207
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:14,000
Çi ger wekî wî.. li derve bin jî we re şa dibin.. we re şa
hebe.
 
Whatever is like him.. even if you are outside, they will be
happy with you.. there is joy with you.

208
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:17,000
Saetên we ji xweş. Ciyê we hate vira..
 
May your hours be pleasant. Your place came here..

209
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:22,000
Û ev silavên me jî li her kesî re.. em jî dibêjin em jî..
sax in, baş in, saet xweş.
 
And these are our greetings to everyone.. we also say we
too.. are alive, well, have a good time.

210
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:25,000
Em rasti dibin saetên we dîsa xweş.
 
We truly say, may your hours be pleasant again.

211
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Û qisûra me hene û of kin û ev hêla dîse cîyê we re.
 
And we have our flaws and pardon them and this side again is
your place.

212
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:33,000
Em divê qisûr tiştan em qisûr nekin...
 
We shouldn't fall short in these things...

213
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:37,000
Em kesî me qesr nekirîne. Û înşelleh em ê nexin.
 
We haven't let anyone down. And God willing, we won't.

214
00:26:37,000 --> 00:26:57,000
Ehlen wa sehlen ji we re, saetên we jî xweş.
 
Welcome to you, may your hours be pleasant too.

215
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:08,000
Xwedê mamoste, wekî dibêjin gotinê xatir.. em xwestin dîya
bike am tiştê zêde.. de, de zêde neke.
 
By God teacher, as they say a parting word.. we wanted to
show it as an extra thing.. come on, don't do extra.

216
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:14,000
As pir kêfxweş bûm min naskirina te. Û destikî, xwestim serê
xwe te ra û wekî te ra bigrim.
 
I was very happy to meet you. And a hand, I wanted to hold
it to my head and to you.

217
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:18,000
Û ew tu gotî basîte... min jî xelkê we nasdike... nas nabe
nas nake.. bibe?
 
And you said it's simple... I too your people know you...
one doesn't get known, doesn't know.. happens?

218
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:29,000
Min got ez biqasîyekî xwedê.. de, qet.. Xwedê we razî be..
Te tiştêkî, pir xweş, xweda jî te de be.. Xwedê ji we razî
be.
 
I said as much as God.. come on, never.. May God be pleased
with you.. You did a very nice thing, may God be in you
too.. May God be pleased with you.

219
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Ahlan wa sahlan ser çavê min bave min. Tu hatî, mîvanên me
re. Ehlen we sahlan.
 
Welcome upon my eyes, my father. You came, to our guests.
Welcome.

220
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:43,000
Û silavê me jî... har yekî, me sêr dike xerîb e an na..
Saetên wê gîya xweş.. û mala wê gîya ava, ahlan wa sahlan.
 
And our greetings too... to everyone, who watches us whether
they are a stranger or not.. May all their hours be
pleasant.. and may all their houses be built, welcome.

221
00:27:43,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Yellah bi selametî bavê Hamo.
 
Come on, go in peace, Bave Hamo.

222
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Ehlê wa sahlan.
 
Welcome.

223
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Ez mezin bûm di vê gundî,
 
I grew up in this village,

224
00:27:53,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Her tiştê xweş min te da dî,
 
I saw every beautiful thing in you,

225
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Çawa sal çûn, emrê me çû,
 
How the years went, our life went,

226
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:12,000
Min nizanî çawa derbas bû.
 
I didn't know how it passed by.

227
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:17,000
Hin di bîra min in, rojên şêrîn,
 
Some of the sweet days are still in my mind,

228
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:23,000
Digerim li wan, wextên şêrîn,
 
I am looking for those sweet times,

229
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:29,000
Çi xweş bû zemanê şahî,
 
How beautiful was the time of joy,

230
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Çima tu zû çûyî ji bîra min.
 
Why did you quickly fade from my memory.

231
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:37,000
Tînim bîra min,
 
I am remembering,

232
00:28:37,000 --> 00:28:42,000
Şefeqê sibê radibûn,
 
We would wake up at the morning dawn,

233
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Dengê dîkan re şa dibûn,
 
We were happy with the sound of the roosters,

234
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:53,000
Hizan û mezin pê re radibûn,
 
The poor and the great woke up to it,

235
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:58,000
Her kes bi karê xwe bû.
 
Everyone was busy with their own work.

236
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:03,000
Yê zû radibû, berê xwe dida kar,
 
Whoever woke up early, set off to work,

237
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:09,000
Civatek xweş û rû li ken bû...
 
It was a pleasant and smiling community...

238
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:14,000
Şivanan pezê xwe, daber dikir,
 
The shepherds were letting their sheep out,

239
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:19,000
Hewal bû, bi xiş û pêl bû...
 
There was a companion, with rustle and movement...

240
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:25,000
Hîn bîra min e...
 
I still remember...

241
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:31,000
Hêviya çavên min,
 
The hope of my eyes,

242
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:36,000
Şevên gundê min...
 
The nights of my village...

243
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Nanê genim, ê tenûr da,
 
The wheat bread, in the tandoor,

244
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:47,000
Digeriyam li nîv şeva...
 
I used to wander in the middle of the night...

245
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:53,000
Mêvaniyê malê... têr nan û av da...
 
The household guests... were given plenty of bread and
water...

246
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:58,000
Dengê xortan û keçan li eywan da.
 
The voice of the young men and women on the balcony.

247
00:29:58,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Bîşenga cama an ji wan re kaniya...
 
A drop of glass or from the fountain for them...

248
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:01,000
...bav û kal.
 
...ancestors.

249
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:04,000
Dixemilîn mal û zavan,
 
The houses of the grooms are decorated,

250
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:07,000
Digerin reqs û dîlan,
 
Dances and halays are held,

251
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:09,000
Gumguma def û fîqan,
 
The echoing of drums and flutes,

252
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:11,000
Şekir reşand ser serê bûkan.
 
Sweets are scattered on the brides' heads.

253
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:14,000
Tê bîra min, tê bîra min,
 
It comes to my mind, it comes to my mind,

254
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:16,000
Ew hevalê min,
 
Those friends of mine,

255
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Narin ji bîra min,
 
They don't fade from my mind,

256
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:23,000
Kuçe û xelkê gundê min.
 
The streets and people of my village.

